s to be the most important aspect of scientific theories. This is not the case, as the critic's argument is focused on the therapeutic success of these theories, not their scientific merit.\n\nOption C suggests that the statement is used to override some considerations against these theories. This is a plausible interpretation, as the critic is arguing that the therapeutic success of these theories outweighs their poor theoretical qualities.\n\nOption D suggests that the statement is used to disprove evidence against these theories. This is not the case, as the critic is not arguing that there is evidence against these theories, but rather that they are successful in producing the right results. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
