messages:    6%|5         | 34/600 [02:11<2:24:52, 15.36s/it][["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nSome students attending a small university with a well-known choir live off campus. From the fact that all music majors are members of the choir, a professor in the music department concluded that none of the students who live off campus is a music major.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, the professor's conclusion is properly drawn if which one of the following is assumed?\n# Options:\nA) None of the students who live off campus is a member of the choir.\nB) All students who are members of the choir are music majors.\nC) Some of the students who do not live off campus are not music majors.\nD) All students who live on campus are music majors.. I think the correct option is: D\n", "<think>.\nTo determine which option is assumed by the professor's conclusion, let's analyze the given information and the conclusion step by step.\n\nThe context states that some students attending a small university with a well-known choir live off campus. Additionally, it is mentioned that all music majors are members of the choir. The professor concludes that none of the students who live off campus is a music major.\n\nNow, let's examine each option:.\n\nA) None of the students who live off campus is a member of the choir.\nThis option contradicts the given information that some students live off campus and are members of the choir. Therefore, this option cannot be assumed.\n\nB) All students who are members of the choir are music majors.\nThis option is consistent with the given information that all music majors are members of the choir. However, it does not directly address the conclusion that none of the students who live off campus is a music major.\n\nC) Some of the students who do not live off campus are not music majors. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
