k, but it does not specify that having a per capita GNP above $4,000 is a sign of developed countries.\n\nC) Many developing countries have experienced violent social shocks in the process of their modernization.\n- This statement is supported by the context. The context mentions that in the modern practice of developing countries, a period of social shock occurs when a country's per capita GNP is between $300 and $4,000. This implies that many developing countries have experienced violent social shocks during their modernization process.\n\nD) Developing countries began industrialization and modernization in an external environment completely different from developed countries.\n- This statement is not directly supported by the context. The context does not mention anything about the external environment in which developing countries began industrialization and modernization. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
