ficiently, it could have better served its purpose. This assumption is not necessary for the argument to hold, as the legislator is only focusing on the job-creation program and its failure.\n\nOption D states that the unemployment rate would not have risen even more than it has if the job-creation program had not been in existence. This assumption is not necessary for the argument to hold, as the legislator is only focusing on the job-creation program and its failure. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
