messages:   25%|##5       | 152/600 [02:56<02:16,  3.29it/s][["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nNearly all employees of the factory who have completed their high school diploma have earned their factory safety certificate, having easily completed the eight week training course. The high school graduates who haven' t earned the certificate are ones who have evening obligations that have prevented them from taking the course. Overall, though, most of the factory workers have not earned the certificate.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, if the statements above are true, which one of the following also must be true?\n# Options:\nA) A large proportion of the factory workers have not graduated from high school.\nB) A large proportion of students with high school diplomas have evening obligations that have prevented them from taking the eight week training course.\nC) Most of the workers who have earned the certificate are high school graduates.\nD) No factory worker without a high school diploma has completed the course and earned the certificate.. I think the correct option is: C\n", "<think>.\nTo determine which statement must be true based on the given information, let's analyze each option step by step:.\n\nA) A large proportion of the factory workers have not graduated from high school.\n- This statement cannot be concluded from the given information. The information only states that nearly all employees with high school diplomas have earned their factory safety certificate, but it does not provide any information about the proportion of workers without high school diplomas.\n\nB) A large proportion of students with high school diplomas have evening obligations that have prevented them from taking the course.\n- This statement can be concluded from the given information. The information states that the high school graduates who haven't earned the certificate are ones who have evening obligations that have prevented them from taking the course. This implies that a large proportion of students with high school diplomas have evening obligations that have prevented them from taking the course.\n\nC) Most of the workers who have earned the certificate are high school graduates.\n- This statement can be concluded from the given information. The information states that nearly all employees with high school diplomas have earned their factory safety certificate. This implies that most of the workers who have earned the certificate are high school graduates. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
