out of the solar system.\n\nNow, let's consider the options:.\n\nA) Jupiter's gravity pushes them into smaller orbits and drives them out of the solar system.\nB) Jupiter's gravity did not push them into smaller orbits, but drove them out of the solar system.\nC) Jupiter's gravity pushed them into smaller orbits, but did not drive them out of the solar system.\nD) Jupiter's gravitational pull neither pushed them into smaller orbits nor drove them out of the solar system.\n\nSince only one of the above two assertions is true, we need to determine which one is true and which one is false.\n\nOption A is true because it matches the first conclusion made by the researchers.\nOption B is true because it matches the second conclusion made by the researchers.\nOption C is true because it matches the first conclusion made by the researchers.\nOption D is true because it matches the second conclusion made by the researchers.\n\nHowever, since only one of the assertions is true, we need to choose the option that is consistent with the given information. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
