messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nDirect selling refers to the business mode in which direct selling enterprises recruit sellers to sell products directly to final consumers outside the fixed business place.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following options is direct selling?\n# Options:\nA) After selecting salesmen, a dairy manufacturer set up 100 sales points in the city to sell dairy products at a unified price.\nB) A bookstore adopts online sales. after customers place an order, the courier will send the products to the designated place and charge a fee.\nC) Some salesmen recruited by a cosmetics brand set up stalls along the road to distribute product descriptions and sell them to customers at lower prices.\nD) At the beginning of school, the new student xiao he bought five table lamps in the wholesale market, one for his own use, and the other four were sold to his classmates.. I think the correct option is: A\n', '<think>.\nTo determine which option represents direct selling, we need to analyze each option based on the definition provided: "Direct selling refers to the business mode in which direct selling enterprises recruit sellers to sell products directly to final consumers outside the fixed business place.".\n\nLet\'s examine each option:.\n\nA) After selecting salesmen, a dairy manufacturer set up 100 sales points in the city to sell dairy products at a unified price.\n- This option involves setting up sales points in the city, which suggests a fixed business place. Therefore, this does not fit the definition of direct selling.\n\nB) A bookstore adopts online sales. After customers place an order, the courier will send the products to the designated place and charge a fee.\n- This option involves online sales, where the products are delivered to the customer\'s location. This is not considered direct selling because the products are not sold directly to the final consumer outside the fixed business place.\n\nC) Some salesmen recruited by a cosmetics brand set up stalls along the road to distribute product descriptions and sell them to customers at lower prices.\n- This option involves salesmen setting up stalls along the road to sell products directly to final consumers. This fits the definition of direct selling because the products are sold directly to the final consumer outside the fixed business place.\n\nD) At the beginning of school, the new student xiao he bought five table lamps in the wholesale market, one for his own use, and the other four were sold to his classmates. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
