messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nInvisible curriculum refers to the informal and unconscious learning experience that is not clearly specified in the school's planned curriculum.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to the above definition, which of the following is not an invisible curriculum?\n# Options:\nA) Colleges and universities organize students to participate in two-day military training to cultivate and exercise students' willpower.\nB) When children learn teaching courses, they cultivate their interest in learning and teaching.\nC) A university set up a university culture festival to let students know the school motto and style of study.\nD) Teachers and students participate in extracurricular activities together to establish an equal and harmonious relationship between teachers and students.. I think the correct option is: D\n", "<think>.\nTo determine which option is not an example of an invisible curriculum, we need to understand what an invisible curriculum is. An invisible curriculum refers to the informal and unconscious learning experiences that are not explicitly taught or specified in the school's planned curriculum. These experiences are often learned through social interactions, cultural norms, and personal experiences.\n\nNow, let's analyze each option:.\n\nA) Colleges and universities organizing students to participate in two-day military training to cultivate and exercise students' willpower - This is an example of an invisible curriculum because it is an informal learning experience that is not explicitly taught in the curriculum but helps students develop important life skills.\n\nB) When children learn teaching courses, they cultivate their interest in learning and teaching - This is also an example of an invisible curriculum because it is an informal learning experience that is not explicitly taught in the curriculum but helps students develop an interest in teaching.\n\nC) A university setting up a university culture festival to let students know the school motto and style of study - This is an example of an invisible curriculum because it is an informal learning experience that is not explicitly taught in the curriculum but helps students understand the school's values and culture. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
