messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nSmithtown University' s fund-raisers succeeded in getting donations from 80 percent of the potential donors they contacted. This success rate, exceptionally high for university fund-raisers, does not indicate that they were doing a good job. On the contrary, since the people most likely to donate are those who have donated in the past, good fund-raisers constantly try less-likely prospects in an effort to expand the donor base. The high success rate shows insufficient canvassing effort.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following, if true, provides more support for the argument?\n# Options:\nA) This year the average size of the donations to smithtown university from new donors when the university's fund-raisers had contacted was larger than the average size of donations from donors who had given to the university before.\nB) The majority of the donations that fund-raisers succeeded in getting for smithtown university this year were from donors who had never given to the university before.\nC) This year most of the donations that came to smithtown university from people who had previously donated to it were made without the university's fund-raisers having made any contact with the donors.\nD) Smithtown university's fund-raisers were successful in their contacts with potential donors who had never given before about as frequently as were fund-raisers for other universities in their contacts with such people.. I think the correct option is: C\n", "<think>.\nThe context states that the high success rate of the fund-raisers at Smithtown University does not indicate that they were doing a good job because the people most likely to donate are those who have donated in the past. This implies that the fund-raisers are not effectively expanding the donor base by trying less-likely prospects. .\n\nNow, let's analyze the options:.\n\nA) This year the average size of the donations to smithtown university from new donors when the university's fund-raisers had contacted was larger than the average size of donations from donors who had given to the university before. This option suggests that the fund-raisers were successful in getting larger donations from new donors, which contradicts the argument that the high success rate shows insufficient canvassing effort. Therefore, this option does not provide support for the argument.\n\nB) The majority of the donations that fund-raisers succeeded in getting for smithtown university this year were from donors who had never given to the university before. This option supports the argument that the fund-raisers are not effectively expanding the donor base by trying less-likely prospects. Therefore, this option provides support for the argument.\n\nC) This year most of the donations that came to smithtown university from people who had previously donated to it were made without the university's fund-raisers having made any contact with the donors. This option suggests that the fund-raisers were not successful in getting donations from previous donors, which contradicts the argument that the high success rate shows insufficient canvassing effort. Therefore, this option does not provide support for the argument.\n\nD) Smithtown university's fund-raisers were successful in their contacts with potential donors who had never given before about as frequently as were fund-raisers for other universities in their contacts with such people. This option suggests that the fund-raisers at Smithtown University were not doing a better job than other universities in getting donations from new donors. Therefore, this option does not provide support for the argument. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
