messages:   57%|#####6    | 340/600 [10:23<02:03,  2.11it/s][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nThe term boundary problem refers to various short-sighted behaviors of employees due to the short employment relationship in modern enterprises, and the harm caused by such behaviors to the enterprise\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the followings belongs to the term boundary problem\n# Options:\nA) Because he will retire in one year, lao zhao feels unable and his work efficiency is getting worse and worse\nB) Because he was not familiar with the business, xiao li, who had just come a month, lost a big customer and the company lost a lot\nC) Because he felt that it was impossible to become a regular worker,xiao wang worked hard every day to show himself \nD) Because he only signed a contract for half a year, xiao sun ignored the use of working machinery and equipment. I think the correct option is: B\n', "<think>.\nTo determine which option belongs to the term boundary problem, we need to analyze each option and see if it demonstrates a short-sighted behavior due to the short employment relationship in modern enterprises. Let's examine each option step by step:.\n\nA) Lao Zhao feels unable because he will retire in one year and his work efficiency is getting worse and worse. This option suggests that Lao Zhao's short-term perspective is affecting his work efficiency, which could be a result of the short employment relationship in modern enterprises. This option seems to fit the definition of the term boundary problem.\n\nB) Xiao Li lost a big customer and the company lost a lot because he was not familiar with the business. This option does not necessarily demonstrate a short-sighted behavior due to the short employment relationship in modern enterprises. It seems more related to Xiao Li's lack of experience and knowledge.\n\nC) Xiao Wang worked hard every day to show himself because he felt that it was impossible to become a regular worker. This option suggests that Xiao Wang's short-term perspective is affecting his work effort, which could be a result of the short employment relationship in modern enterprises. This option also seems to fit the definition of the term boundary problem.\n\nD) Xiao Sun ignored the use of working machinery and equipment because he only signed a contract for half a year. This option does not necessarily demonstrate a short-sighted behavior due to the short employment relationship in modern enterprises. It seems more related to Xiao Sun's lack of understanding of the company's policies.\n\nBased on the analysis, options A and C seem to fit the definition of the term boundary problem. However, since the question asks for the correct option, we should choose the one that is most directly related to the term boundary problem. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
