messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nOur parents pay more and more attention to children's reading. Most parents want their children to read more and read better books. In 2018,70.3 percent of families in one city had the habit of parents reading with their children. The amount of books read by parents and children increased by 1.8 percentage points compared to 2017 and the length of books read also increased compared to last year. But in 2018, the city's children read just 4.72 books per person, down 0.6 percentage points from 2017.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following, if true, best explains the phenomenon?\n# Options:\nA) In recent years, children have a heavy burden of schoolwork and many people want to read extracurricular reading but do not have enough time.\nB) Most parents born in the 1980s and 1990s are highly educated and value reading for their children.\nC) Many children are used to listening to books in parent-child reading, which is not counted in 2018.\nD) Electronic reading by parents on mobile phones and computers has not been taken into account in children's books.. I think the correct option is: B\n", '<think>.\nTo determine which option best explains the phenomenon of children reading just 4.72 books per person in 2018, we need to consider the context provided and analyze each option step by step.\n\nOption A suggests that children have a heavy burden of schoolwork and lack time for extracurricular reading. This could potentially explain why children are reading fewer books, as they may not have enough free time to engage in reading activities. However, this option does not directly address the issue of parents reading with their children and the increase in the amount of books read by parents and children. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
