messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nThe law of tea production in the world is red in the south and green in the north, that is, only high quality black tea can be produced in lower latitudes (such as India and Kenya), while high quality green tea can be produced in relatively high latitudes (25  degree~ 30  degreenorth latitude). The international price of green tea has always been higher than that of black tea. The quality of green tea in India, Indonesia and Sri Lanka, the main tea producing countries, is not high. Since the 1970s, the above three countries began to change red to green in an attempt to occupy the international green tea market, all of which ended in failure. China's famous green tea is mainly distributed in mountainous areas. with rich rural labor resources and low labor costs, the development of green tea industry has obvious comparative advantages.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following statements is consistent with the original text?\n# Options:\nA) At present, the supply of black tea exceeds the demand in the international market\nB) The price of indian green tea is higher than the international average price of green tea\nC) Chinese green tea has competitive strength in the international market\nD) There is a trend of change red to green in the international tea market. I think the correct option is: D\n", '<think>.\nTo determine which statement is consistent with the original text, let\'s analyze each option step by step:.\n\nA) At present, the supply of black tea exceeds the demand in the international market.\n- The text mentions that "red in the south and green in the north" indicates that high-quality black tea is produced in lower latitudes like India and Kenya, while high-quality green tea is produced in higher latitudes like China. However, it does not explicitly state whether the supply of black tea exceeds the demand in the international market. Therefore, this statement cannot be confirmed as consistent with the original text.\n\nB) The price of Indian green tea is higher than the international average price of green tea.\n- The text states that "the quality of green tea in India, Indonesia, and Sri Lanka, the main tea producing countries, is not high." This implies that the price of Indian green tea might not necessarily be higher than the international average price of green tea. Thus, this statement cannot be confirmed as consistent with the original text.\n\nC) Chinese green tea has competitive strength in the international market.\n- The text mentions that "Chinese green tea is mainly distributed in mountainous areas with rich rural labor resources and low labor costs, which gives the development of green tea industry obvious comparative advantages." This suggests that Chinese green tea has competitive strengths in the international market due to its favorable labor conditions. Therefore, this statement can be considered consistent with the original text.\n\nD) There is a trend of change red to green in the international tea market.\n- The text states that "since the 1970s, the above three countries began to change red to green in an attempt to occupy the international green tea market, all of which ended in failure." This indicates that there was a trend of changing red to green in the international tea market, but it did not succeed. Therefore, this statement can be considered consistent with the original text.\n\nBased on the analysis, both options C and D can be considered consistent with the original text. However, since the question asks for the correct option, I will choose the one that directly addresses the statement about Chinese green tea having competitive strength in the international market.\n\n<｜User｜>. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
