messages:   68%|######8   | 408/600 [12:54<00:37,  5.09it/s][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nVirtual team refers to a community composed of two or more people across regions and organizations. They are connected through communication and information technology. They have complementary technologies or skills, common goals, common evaluation and work methods, and they jointly bear the final results and responsibilities.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to the above definition, which one of the followings belongs to a virtual team?\n# Options:\nA) A publishing firm contacted several experts to jointly compile a new textbook. they work in different units and coordinating their work is mainly through telephone, fax and network.\nB) A company transferred each two key employees from the sales department, r&d department and production department to form a new product research team.\nC) Xiao li encountered technical problems in his work. he was not familiar with a professional field. he consulted many experts through the internet and telephone, and established regular and fixed contacts with the experts.\nD) Xiao tang, xiao sun and xiao liu often chat on the internet and find that they have similar experiences and common hobbies. so they become good friends.. I think the correct option is: B\n', "<think>.\nTo determine which option belongs to a virtual team, we need to identify the key characteristics of a virtual team mentioned in the context. These characteristics include:.\n\n1. Complementary technologies or skills.\n2. Common goals.\n3. Common evaluation and work methods.\n4. Jointly bear the final results and responsibilities.\n\nNow let's analyze each option:.\n\nA) A publishing firm contacted several experts to jointly compile a new textbook. They work in different units and coordinating their work is mainly through telephone, fax, and network. This option meets the criteria of a virtual team because it involves multiple experts working together on a common goal (compiling a new textbook) using technology to coordinate their work.\n\nB) A company transferred each two key employees from the sales department, R&D department, and production department to form a new product research team. This option does not meet the criteria of a virtual team because it involves employees from the same company working together in a physical location.\n\nC) Xiao Li encountered technical problems in his work. He was not familiar with a professional field. He consulted many experts through the internet and telephone, and established regular and fixed contacts with the experts. This option does not meet the criteria of a virtual team because it involves an individual seeking help from experts, rather than a group of people working together on a common goal.\n\nD) Xiao Tang, Xiao Sun, and Xiao Liu often chat on the internet and find that they have similar experiences and common hobbies. So they become good friends. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
