e perception of color persists even after the object has been removed. This is an example of a positive image, as the original color is retained temporarily.\n\nC) After staring at red for a long time, the vision moves quickly to white, not white, but green.\nThis option describes a phenomenon where the perception of color changes from red to green. This is an example of a negative image, as the original color is replaced by a different color.\n\nD) Red is paired with yellow, and red is sometimes seen as a color with purple, and sometimes with yellow as a color with green.\nThis option describes a phenomenon where the perception of color changes based on the context or the presence of other colors. This is not related to the concept of continuous contrast or positive/negative images. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
