messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nComets do not give off their own light but reflect light from other sources, such as the Sun. Scientists estimate the mass of comets by their brightness: the greater a comet' s mass, the more light that comet will reflect. A satellite probe, however, has revealed that the material of which Halley' s comet is composed reflects 60 times less light per unit of mass than had been previously thought.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, the statements above, if true, give the most support to which one of the following?\n# Options:\nA) The reflective properties of the material of which comets are composed vary considerably from comet to comet.\nB) Previous estimates of the mass of halley's comet which were based on its brightness were too low.\nC) The total amount of light reflected from halley's comet is less than scientists had previously thought.\nD) Scientists need more information before they can make a good estimate of the mass of halley's comet.. I think the correct option is: C\n", "<think>.\nTo determine the correct answer, let's analyze each option based on the given context and information:.\n\nA) The reflective properties of the material of which comets are composed vary considerably from comet to comet.\n- The context mentions that the material of which Halley's comet is composed reflects 60 times less light per unit of mass than had been previously thought. This suggests that the reflective properties of comets may vary, but it doesn't necessarily mean that they vary considerably from comet to comet. The context only provides information about Halley's comet, so we cannot generalize this to all comets.\n\nB) Previous estimates of the mass of Halley's comet which were based on its brightness were too low.\n- The context states that the satellite probe revealed that the material of which Halley's comet is composed reflects 60 times less light per unit of mass than had been previously thought. This implies that the previous estimates of the mass of Halley's comet were indeed too low, as the new information suggests that the comet is more massive than previously thought.\n\nC) The total amount of light reflected from Halley's comet is less than scientists had previously thought.\n- The context mentions that the satellite probe revealed that the material of which Halley's comet is composed reflects 60 times less light per unit of mass than had been previously thought. This suggests that the total amount of light reflected from Halley's comet is indeed less than scientists had previously thought.\n\nD) Scientists need more information before they can make a good estimate of the mass of Halley's comet. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
