ncentrations of natural drugs and synthetic pesticides.\n\nB) Humans have been ingesting the natural drugs contained in these plants for thousands of years and have time to adapt to them.\n- This option undermines the argument because it suggests that humans have adapted to the natural drugs over time, making them less harmful. This implies that the harm caused by synthetic pesticides is not as significant as previously thought.\n\nC) The chemical structure of synthetic pesticides is usually simpler than that of natural drugs contained in plants.\n- This option does not undermine the argument because it does not directly address the harm caused by synthetic pesticides. It only compares the chemical structures of synthetic pesticides and natural drugs.\n\nD) Natural drugs contained in plants are usually only suitable for resisting specific organisms, while synthetic pesticides are usually harmful to a variety of organisms.\n- This option undermines the argument because it suggests that natural drugs are less harmful than synthetic pesticides because they are specific to certain organisms. This implies that the harm caused by synthetic pesticides is not as significant as previously thought. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
