mity to water is good for both body and mind, as it shows a positive correlation between frequent visits to the seaside and improved mental health.\n\nB) Studies have shown that staying in an urban environment makes people more likely to feel tired and depressed.\n- This option contradicts the conclusion that proximity to water is good for both body and mind, as it suggests that urban environments are detrimental to mental health, which is contrary to the context's claim about the benefits of green spaces.\n\nC) The aquatic environment has unique and favorable environmental factors, such as less air pollution and more sunshine. People living near the water tend to participate more actively in physical exercise, such as water sports and walking, and it also has the role of psychological rehabilitation.\n- This option supports the conclusion that proximity to water is good for both body and mind, as it highlights the unique environmental factors and physical activities associated with aquatic environments that contribute to improved health.\n\nD) Studies have shown that staying in or near an aquatic environment can stimulate positive emotions and reduce negative emotions and stress compared with green spaces. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
