he context.\n\n3. **Option C**: "Some new scientific discoveries do not represent, on a deep level, a variation on previous themes.".\n   - The context explicitly states that "what we choose to call a new theme or a new discovery is itself always and without exception some sort of variation, on a deep level, of previous themes." This statement contradicts the context.\n\n4. **Option D**: "No scientific idea is entirely independent of all other ideas.".\n   - The context implies that every idea is built upon a thousand related ideas, suggesting that no scientific idea is entirely independent of all other ideas. This statement aligns with the context. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
