ironment because of the difficulty in studying it, rather than the accuracy of the technology.\n\nB) This option discusses the movement of currents on the ocean floor, which is not directly related to the difficulty in studying the sea floor. It does not address the main point of the context.\n\nC) This option claims that sea-level temperature conditions are generally stable and consistent because sunlight cannot penetrate deep below sea level. While this is true, it does not directly address the difficulty in studying the sea floor.\n\nD) This option states that very few people have seen detailed maps of sea floor extensions, even though such maps can be seen in almost every major library. This suggests that the lack of knowledge about the sea floor is due to the limited availability of information, not the difficulty in studying it. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
