rs accustomed to regular exercise do not gain weight when they stop exercising.\nThis option suggests that nonsmokers who are accustomed to regular exercise do not gain weight when they stop exercising. This information could be relevant to understanding the potential benefits of exercise for people trying to quit smoking, as it implies that exercise can help maintain a healthy weight. This option supports the argument.\n\nD) Aerobic exercise can stimulate the brain's production of endorphins, which reduce tension.\nThis option suggests that aerobic exercise can stimulate the brain's production of endorphins, which can reduce tension. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
