y - This option suggests that as people age, their body fluids become less watery, which could potentially lead to a less dramatic temperature change. However, this doesn't directly explain why heat stroke is more likely to occur in young children in a car compared to adults.\n\nC) The car belongs to a confined space, when the outdoor temperature reaches, the car temperature can be reached, and adults in the car is likely to open the window when they feel uncomfortable - This option suggests that the confined space of a car can trap heat, leading to a higher temperature inside the car. However, this doesn't directly explain why heat stroke is more likely to occur in young children in a car compared to adults.\n\nD) Heat stroke usually occurs when you lose your body weight in water. young children have a larger body surface area to absorb heat more quickly, and because they have the same number of sweat glands as adults, they lose water more quickly - This option suggests that young children have a larger body surface area, which allows them to absorb heat more quickly. Additionally, they have the same number of sweat glands as adults, which means they lose water more quickly. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
